ifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the leaf's push-mode LIVE per-call carve-out (AC2) with parent eb64's unconditional 'consumers do not reread ambient configuration during the operation' invariant: either amend the parent AC/Outcome C to enumerate the push-mode exception (staling and re-triggering the parent's plan review) or confirm and bound the exception so the parent's compose-once contract still holds as stated.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.63,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Leaf AC2: 'Push mode is a documented, tested exception: it stays LIVE per-call because `_io/import_ndjson.py` toggles `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` mid-bulk-import ... The new tests assert this carve-out explicitly (push mode observes the mutation even inside a bound operation)'","Parent eb64 Outcome C: 'An operation composes once; downstream code consumes projections/context and cannot reread environment, files, or CWD.'","Parent eb64 AC: 'CLI, MCP, Python, shared command/store, and LLM operations compose one authoritative snapshot/context; behavior-bearing consumers do not reread ambient configuration during the operation.'","The exception is grounded in a real existing coupling (test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py), so the parent's core config-authority goal still holds; this is a documented, tested carve-out the parent AC simply does not enumerate rather than a gratuitous scope expansion -> incomplete_enumeration."],"finding":"Leaf AC2 carves out a push-mode LIVE per-call exception (REBAR_SYNC_PUSH is reread mid-operation), which is a behavior-bearing consumer rereading ambient configuration during the operation -- something the parent epic's Outcome C ('downstream code ... cannot reread environment, files, or CWD') and parent AC ('behavior-bearing consumers do not reread ambient configuration during the operation') state unconditionally, without enumerating this exception.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7370dde1aca7f617","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2 (push-mode carve-out); parent eb64 Outcome C and its config AC","norm_id":"n652de8b618e975ce","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer reconciling the leaf's landed behavior against the parent epic's compose-once/no-reread invariant will find an undocumented divergence at the parent level.","The parent's final epic-evidence AC ('reports ... ambient authorities') must account for the push-mode live-read as a deliberate, bounded residual authority."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add an explicit push-mode carve-out clause to parent eb64's Outcome C / config AC (e.g. 'except REBAR_SYNC_PUSH, which remains a live per-call read to preserve the import_ndjson bulk-push coupling'), so the leaf's AC2 is a documented subset of an updated parent contract rather than an unenumerated relaxation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'tracker_dir/tickets_branch/tickets_remote in config.py now consult the bound snapshot via _bound_snapshot_for_root before falling back to load_config'","config.py:145-159 tracker_dir calls load_config(root) directly; :172 tickets_branch returns load_config(root).tracker.branch; :187 tickets_remote returns load_config(root).sync.remote — no snapshot path","search for `_bound_snapshot_for_root` repo-wide returns (no matches)"],"finding":"AC4 asserts tracker_dir/tickets_branch/tickets_remote in config.py 'now consult the bound snapshot via _bound_snapshot_for_root before falling back to load_config', but reading config.py (lines 138-188) shows all three functions call load_config directly with no snapshot consultation, and `_bound_snapshot_for_root` has zero matches anywhere in the repo.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8fb897c962a5d9fb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC4 (store helpers / config.py)","norm_id":"na95fc26ab9d6782e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'The reconciler runtime already demonstrates snapshot-derived bindings; reuse that pattern.'","AC1: 'the new `bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools` MCP proxy all bind exactly one snapshot per outer call and reuse it for nested seams'","AC2 push carve-out: '`_io/import_ndjson.py` toggles `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` mid-bulk-import ... freezing push mode would silently break that existing ... coupling'","src/rebar/_opcert_binding.py:42-53 already defines `_BOUND`/`_PUSH_MODE` ContextVars with `current_binding()`, `current_push_mode()`, and `bound_signer(...)` (reentrant, finally-reset), whose module docstring notes it isolates concurrent workers and falls back to `resolve_push_mode` when push_mode is unbound — the exact push carve-out AC2 describes.","The plan names only the reconciler runtime as prior art and does not reference `_opcert_binding`."],"finding":"The plan proposes a new ambient per-operation 'bound snapshot' carrier (`bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools`, `_bound_snapshot_for_root` consulted inside config.py with compose-once/reentrancy) but never mentions the existing `rebar._opcert_binding` ContextVar binding, which already provides per-operation binding with reentrancy + finally-reset and even a push-mode carve-out for the same REBAR_SYNC_PUSH live-read concern the plan's AC2 raises. It is unclear whether the new binding reuses that carrier or duplicates it (NIH).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae75c4ae745b8bfe","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('reuse that pattern'); Acceptance Criteria AC1 (`bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools`), AC2 (push-mode carve-out), AC4 (`_bound_snapshot_for_root`)","norm_id":"nc575d1b608ea8655","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In Approach/Scope, cite `src/rebar/_opcert_binding.py` and specify whether `bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools`/`_bound_snapshot_for_root` add a snapshot to the existing binding carrier (reusing its reentrancy + `_PUSH_MODE` fallback) or introduce a new ContextVar; if new, give the affirmative reason the existing carrier cannot host the snapshot.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the new bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools MCP proxy all bind exactly one snapshot per outer call and reuse it for nested seams'","AC2: 'a new operation observes the change' implies rebinding per operation but the retirement/clearing mechanism is not named","ABSENCE: no statement of contextvar vs thread-local vs module-global storage, nor concurrency isolation between simultaneous MCP tool calls on a shared server process"],"finding":"The plan introduces a per-operation bound OperationSnapshot (via _main_dispatch, the bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools MCP proxy, and append_event) but never specifies the storage mechanism (contextvar, thread-local, or module global) or how the binding is cleared/retired between operations. For a long-lived MCP server that may handle concurrent or interleaved operations, an unspecified storage discipline risks one operation's snapshot leaking into a concurrent operation (a check-then-act / cross-request contamination TOCTOU), or a binding accumulating rather than retiring after its operation completes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8a513106cd764b53","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'Compose exactly once after input parsing and before lock/network/write, then pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams'; AC1 bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools MCP proxy","norm_id":"n022fd0e8b7dbd252","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that the binding is stored in a contextvar (or equivalent per-operation scope) that is entered before compose and reset when the outer call returns, and add a test that interleaves two operations with different repository roots to prove no cross-contamination and clean retirement.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams' (explicit threading) vs 'reuse that [reconciler] pattern'.","AC4: '`tracker_dir`/`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote` in `config.py` now consult the bound snapshot via `_bound_snapshot_for_root` before falling back to `load_config`' — an ambient lookup, not a threaded argument.","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py:231-249 `compose_reconciler_runtime` returns a runtime that is threaded explicitly; nothing in config.py-equivalent is consulted ambiently in that pattern."],"finding":"The Approach cites the reconciler runtime as the pattern to reuse, but that pattern EXPLICITLY THREADS the composed object through call arguments (compose_reconciler_runtime returns a ReconcilerRuntime passed to build_backend), whereas the ACs implement an AMBIENT lookup consulted from inside config.py helpers (`_bound_snapshot_for_root` inside `tracker_dir`/`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote`). The plan does not reconcile 'thread focused context' with 'config.py 